# PX4 parameters of the DroneRL drone on top of the x500 airframe. sim/sitl.sh loads them in SITL,
# in M5 the same set goes to the drone. Indoor hall (plan/M4.md, D2): optical flow and a downward
# ToF rangefinder, no GPS.
SYS_HAS_GPS 0
EKF2_GPS_CTRL 0
EKF2_OF_CTRL 1
# flat hall floor: the rangefinder holds the height better than the barometer indoors
EKF2_RNG_CTRL 2
EKF2_HGT_REF 2
# the SITL barometer drifts by decimetres and dragged the height away from the rangefinder (M4.7)
EKF2_BARO_CTRL 0
# no external vision on the drone, ground truth must not reach the EKF
EKF2_EV_CTRL 0
# sensor positions in the body frame (FRD) as in sim/gazebo/models/x500_dronerl
EKF2_OF_POS_X 0.03
EKF2_OF_POS_Z 0.1
EKF2_RNG_POS_Z 0.05
# the companion talks to PX4 over DDS, not MAVLink, so no ground station link is expected
NAV_DLL_ACT 0
# flight height of the contract
MIS_TAKEOFF_ALT 1.2
# offboard loss: Position mode, so a pilot with RC holds the drone (M5); without RC the action of RC
# loss applies, Land, as Return would climb to RTL_RETURN_ALT once the EKF has a global origin
COM_OF_LOSS_T 1.0
COM_OBL_RC_ACT 0
NAV_RCL_ACT 3
# hard geofence behind the soft one of safety_node: landing at a breach of the cylinder around home
# (GF_MAX_HOR_DIST from the map, sim.launch.py) or of the ceiling; it needs the global origin that
# mission_node gives the EKF
GF_ACTION 5
GF_MAX_VER_DIST 2.5
# Return, still left to some failsafes, stays at the flight height indoors
RTL_RETURN_ALT 1.2
RTL_DESCEND_ALT 1.2
